This is a placeholder for the PolyHandle.cur cursor file. 

Since cursor files (.cur) are binary resources and I cannot access the original file content from the repository, this is a migration note.

The original PolyHandle.cur file needs to be manually copied from the .NET 4.8 project to this location in the .NET 9 project.

This cursor file is used by:
- DrawPolygon.cs in the LoadCursor() method
- DrawConnector.cs in the LoadCursor() method

The cursor is loaded using: handleCursor = new Cursor(GetType(), "PolyHandle.cur");

For .NET 9 with SkiaSharp migration, the cursor loading mechanism will remain the same since Windows Forms cursors are not part of System.Drawing and do not need to be replaced with SkiaSharp equivalents.

The cursor file should be included as an EmbeddedResource in the .NET 9 project file.